WEBVTT

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.250
It's going to be another cold day.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.920
You must really like that sleeping bag.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.660
It's warm, isn't it?

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.870
I should really put it away.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.010
Aki-chan

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.270
Who's up for going camping this next break?

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.200
Camping!

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:23.240
<b>(2) Episode 5 
Caribou-kun and Lake Yamanaka</b>

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.630
Mt. Fuji Station...

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.240
We made it!

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:27.040
Check out the huge torii!

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.410
It's so cold.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.900
Looks like it snowed again yesterday.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.730
Good thing we're bundled up.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.220
Yeah.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:43.100
We took a pretty big detour 
getting here by train.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:48.520
We went from Kofu to Ohtsuki, then did a 
lap around to make it to Mt. Fuji Station.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.770
Yeah.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.180
Aki-chan, what's our next step?

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.560
There's a tour bus that leaves from here.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.030
We'll take that to—

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:07.160
E-Ena, help...

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.540
Let's see...

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:17.130
An all-access pass for Lake Yamanaka, please.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.540
That'll be 1,500 yen each.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:23.550
<b>Fujiyoshida/Oshino/Lake Yamanaka Area</b>

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:23.550
Wow, two days of free access to the buses.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:27.380
We could go sightseeing around Lake 
Yamanaka before we go to the campsite.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:30.120
Hang on...

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.900
Take a look at the schedule.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:38.000
Six laps around Lake Yamanaka clockwise, 
five laps counter-clockwise...

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.180
We won't get to look around much 
before it makes its last trip.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.450
Right?

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:46.240
But you can leave this to me.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.200
I've come up with the perfect plan.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.480
Wait, the bus is already here!

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:53.740
Hurry up, kids!

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:56.580
We'll have to wait another 
hour if we miss this one!

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.460
You just said you had a perfect plan!

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:01.510
<i>The door is now closing.</i>

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:10.740
Thank goodness we got a seat.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.350
All according to plan.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:14.710
So where are we getting off?

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:21.220
We'll stop by Fujiyoshida Caribou, 
then head to a hot spring at Lake Yamanaka.

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:25.050
Then we'll go grocery shopping,
and then we'll arrive at the campsite.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:27.240
Tomorrow, we'll go sightseeing 
around Lake Yamanaka.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.630
Great job working in the hot spring, Aki.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:33.370
But of course.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:40.240
Too bad Nadeshiko-chan and Rin-chan are 
working. Even Sensei couldn't make it.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:44.160
That's just how it is. It's hard to get 
everyone's time off to line up.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:51.020
Nothing beats camping while 
other people are working...

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:54.580
I'm gonna send them pics as 
soon as we get to the campsite!

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:56.250
You're evil.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.180
Yup, evil.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:03.780
I'm glad Nadeshiko-chan found a job, though.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.410
Let's go visit her sometime.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.530
<b>Fujimoto
Hand-made soba</b>

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:14.640
Excuse me!

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.160
May we order?

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.790
Sure! I'll be right over.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.460
<b>Caribou</b>

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.460
<b>Fuji Beer Hall</b>

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.460
<b>Fujiyoshida Udon Hall</b>

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.460
<b>Mt. Fuji Radar Dome</b>

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:24.300
<i>Now arriving at Mt. Fuji Radar Dome.
This is Mt. Fuji Radar Dome.</i>

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.560
It sure is cold.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.550
I know.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:38.310
No wonder this place is a summer resort.

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.670
It's a waystation.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:45.710
It says "Fuji Beer Hall."

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:47.570
Sensei would love this place.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:50.320
We're here.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.000
It's huge!

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.340
It looks even bigger than 
the Caribou in Minobu.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:55.310
Yup.

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:58.150
It's the biggest factory outlet 
in the area, apparently.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:01.460
It's Caribou-kun!

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.460
Caribou-kun?

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:05.840
<b>Mascot
Caribou-kun</b>

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.730
So fluffy...

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:18.000
It really is.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.830
Sheesh, you're such kids.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:22.560
Don't go glomping it.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.480
Why not?

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.740
Come on, let's get going.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:29.870
<i>My legs...</i>

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:31.020
<i>They won't move!</i>

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:32.740
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:36.750
<i>Am I in range of its powers?</i>

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:38.750
<i>No!</i>

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.750
<i>It's drawing me in!</i>

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:44.830
You glomped it, too.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:53.830
Maybe it's because we're close to Mt. Fuji,
 but there's a lot of hiking gear.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:56.540
This is the same sleeping bag I have.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:57.660
Hey, hey...

00:06:58.260 --> 00:06:59.890
Isn't this pretty nice?

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.260
Fancy cookware.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:06.400
It looks like a Northern European wood pot.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:10.130
Or so I thought, but it's plastic.

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:11.160
You're right.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:12.390
Yup.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.910
That's why I like it. It'd be easy to care for.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.100
Huh?

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.420
What happened to your wood bowl from before?

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:18.960
<i>Gulp!</i>

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:23.170
Oh, yeah. You oiled it, but then 
didn't use it at our Christmas camp.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:25.830
Oh, yeah, that...

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:28.310
It's been through some hard times.

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:31.930
It's currently living happily as a cactus pot.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:36.370
That reminds me, Inuko!
What about your chair?

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:37.860
You said you were gonna buy one.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:39.810
Oh, right!

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:45.360
I'm thinking one of these two.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.570
A high chair or a low chair, huh?

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:52.710
<i>Camp chairs come in either
 the "high" or "low" style.</i>

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.830
<i>High chairs are raised off the ground,</i>

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:59.950
<i>making it easy to cook or work 
with campfires while seated.</i>

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.020
<i>Low chairs sit closer to the ground,</i>

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:05.080
<i>making them ideal for lounging.</i>

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.450
I can't decide.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:10.520
They're about the same price, too.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.210
Just buy both.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:14.090
That's crazy.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.740
Do you not need a chair, Aki-chan?

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:17.600
Me?

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:21.070
I want a hammock, actually.

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:23.080
Hammocks are nice.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.100
Yeah, but...

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:27.360
The ones with frames are too heavy,

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:30.560
and without a frame, it's hard 
to find a place to hang them up.

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:34.310
So I'm kind of stuck.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:35.860
Are you looking for something?

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:42.640
A hammock that's light and 
stands on its own, huh?

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:45.620
Ideally around 10,000 yen, if possible.

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:49.640
The lightest one we have is six kilograms.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:51.380
Six kilograms is a bit heavy...

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:56.890
I don't know if we carry anything lighter.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:08:59.250
How about...

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:01.800
I see people do this at campsites sometimes.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:04.640
You put two of these together, and...

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:08.150
Why not use them like this?

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:13.370
Thank you.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:17.160
Look what we bought.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:21.310
Aren't you buying anything, Ena?

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:22.460
Not me.

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:26.420
I bought a tent for Chikuwa the 
other day, so I think I'm good.

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.740
It arrived yesterday.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:32.690
You bought a dog tent.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:34.050
Chikuwa in a tent!

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:35.790
How cute.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:41.540
Come on, Aki, that's enough glomping.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:44.680
All right.

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:47.370
It's a bit early, but the hot spring is next!

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:48.410
Hot spring!

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:50.020
Hot spring!

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:56.190
<b>Takeda Bookstore</b>

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:03.700
<b>Chill, fancy camping style</b>

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:03.700
<i>That's right... They're going camping today.</i>

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:10.630
<i>I wonder where they've headed.</i>

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:18.230
This hot spring's perfect.

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:19.530
I know.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:24.560
Such a nice view of Mt. Fuji.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:26.270
Yeah.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.650
Hot springs are best in the winter.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:34.900
But sweating it out in one 
during the summer is nice, too.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.030
That's true.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:42.890
In other words, hot springs 
are good all year round.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.360
I'm so glad I came.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:50.480
Were you on the fence about it, Ena?

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:52.290
Oh, no.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:55.010
I was kinda surprised myself,

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:58.420
but when I saw the word "camping," 
I jumped on it immediately.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:02.630
That last trip was just so much fun.

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:15.360
All right, we're gonna have an even better Lake Yamanaka trip this time!

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.230
You're so gung-ho.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.570
Well, let's get going.

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:23.060
Before we turn into prunes.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:24.680
Yeah.

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:31.420
Aren't you getting out, Aki-chan?

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:33.770
Aren't <i>you</i>, Ena?

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:38.590
Outdoor temp: 1.4°C

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:38.590
Water temp: 38°C

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.590
<i>It's so warm, I can't get out...</i>

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:42.040
All right, we'll all get out 
on the count of three.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:43.470
Okay.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:44.470
Three...

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:45.470
Two...

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:46.850
One!

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:50.450
It's so cold!

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.850
That evaporative cooling!

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:53.850
Wait...

00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:56.860
You traitors!

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:02.960
Wanna grab something to eat?

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:04.360
Okay.

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:08.420
Hey.

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:10.620
They have Kikyou Shingen soft serve.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:14.880
<b>Kikyou Shingen Soft Serve
Matcha
450 yen</b>

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:14.880
<b>Kikyou Shingen Soft Serve
Vanilla
450 yen</b>

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:12.110
Oh, yeah.

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:13.820
I'm gonna have that.

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:14.880
Me, too.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:28.990
It's kind of become a ritual to get 
ice cream before our camping trips, huh?

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:34.390
This kinako rice cake and 
ice cream go together so perfectly.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:38.430
Aoi-chan, want to try my matcha ice cream?

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:41.400
Wanna try some of my vanilla, then?

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:45.920
<i>Yup.</i>

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:47.700
<i>Pretty good.</i>

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:52.010
So where's our campsite today?

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:54.470
Oh, Aki should...

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.540
Huh? Where's Aki?

00:12:57.270 --> 00:12:59.240
Nyum.

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:00.420
Such bad manners!

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:01.640
Come on!

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:06.150
It's gonna be Hottokeya Hot Springs 
all over again if you pass out here.

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:11.120
You too, Ena-chan?!

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:13.930
Kiritanpo?

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:14.830
Yeah.

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:16.870
We're having kiritanpo hot pot tonight.

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:18.970
It's a popular hot pot in the north.

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:20.940
It'll warm you right up.

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:24.440
I've never had kiritanpo before.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:25.950
Me, either.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.460
Same.

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:28.940
Wait, you haven't?

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:34.700
Do they sell kiritanpo at the supermarket?

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:39.280
How naïve, Ena.

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:41.210
Does Nobunaga not always say,

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:46.150
"If you have none, make some kiritanpo"?

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.340
Da!

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:49.720
Nah, he never said that.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:54.470
How to make kiritanpo

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.300
<i>How to make kiritanpo.</i>

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:58.440
<i>Grind rice, pat on some salt water,</i>

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.350
<b>Knead</b>

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.350
<b>Knead</b>

00:13:56.350 --> 00:14:00.110
Salt water

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.110
Streeetch

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:02.870
<i>wrap it around a stick, 
and cook it in a pan until browned.</i>

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:03.610
Hot!

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:03.570
Hot!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:07.360
<i>Remove it from the stick, 
cut it to size, and you're finished.</i>

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:08.320
All done!

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:08.610
All done!

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:12.870
Let's see...

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:17.120
Carrots, burdock root, Japanese parsley, 
maitake mushrooms, green onions...

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:21.190
Maybe we should have prepped 
the veggies ahead of time.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:23.370
It's going to be a pain doing 
the peeling and stuff.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:24.630
Oh, about that...

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:27.130
We'll be using this.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:35.520
<b>Hearty Pork Miso
Soup Add-ins</b>

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:35.520
Contains pork

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:35.520
Burdock root, carrot, daikon, shiitake, green onion, taro root, yam cake, pork

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:35.520
Burdock root, carrots, daikon, 
shiitake mushrooms, green onions...

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:36.710
You're right.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:39.020
It's almost the same ingredients.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.090
Right?

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:41.520
That's clever, Aki-chan.

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:45.490
Actually, Nadeshiko taught me this yesterday.

00:14:45.490 --> 00:14:48.030
Oh, so it was Nadeshiko-chan.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:49.570
About making kiritanpo...

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.440
You can fry it on its own,

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:54.220
but it's even better with sesame oil!

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:59.960
Also, you can make your 
hot pot soup with soy sauce,

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:03.120
but I'd recommend a 
creamy sesame milk soup.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:05.300
Sesame milk sounds good.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:09.100
Oh, and if you don't have Japanese 
parsley, you can use honeywort.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:12.190
Also, chicken breast gets too tough,

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:14.480
so I'd recommend thighs or chicken meatballs.

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:15.650
Oh!

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:20.440
And you can grate some Chinese yam 
for sesame milk yam kiritanpo hot pot!

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:23.850
Nadeshiko-chan's a real
hot pot (<i>nabe</i>) master, huh?

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:25.320
That's our Nabeshiko-chan.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:30.270
<i>Hot pot fairy, Nabeshiko-chan!</i>

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:31.530
Hot pot fairy
 Nabeshiko-chan

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:35.560
All right. I shall make Nabeshiko my wife.

00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:38.220
No, Aki-chan!

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:41.130
Nabeshiko is to be <i>my</i> bride!

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:42.960
Uh, what's going on here?

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:46.080
Then Nabeshiko will be wife to us all.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:49.710
And we'll have tasty hot pot 
whenever we want!

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:55.780
Hip, hip, hooray!

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:57.370
What's even happening?

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:01.500
Soup, add-ins, rice... All set.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:02.730
I think that's everything.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:06.540
And we can buy a pestle at 
the 100-yen shop next door.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:07.710
Right.

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.240
Hey, guys...

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:11.210
Why don't we buy these?

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:12.990
Lake smelt

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:12.990
Oh, lake smelt.

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:16.290
Huh, they sell lake smelt here?

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:17.220
Oh, yeah.

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:20.250
Lake Yamanaka's famous for being 
a lake smelt fishing spot.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.180
Remember that video we 
watched at our Christmas camp?

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:24.750
The lake smelt fishing competition?

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:27.380
Oh, yeah, you're right.

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:29.740
<i>Well, well! Eat up! Eat up!</i>

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:33.540
Let's try making lake smelt 
tempura like they did.

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:35.390
Yeah, that sounds good.

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:39.330
Cleaning up might be a pain, though.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.560
With the used oil and stuff.

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:46.520
We can pour the oil into a 
plastic bottle and take it home.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:48.260
Oh, good idea.

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:51.280
We'll have to buy tempura 
batter and sauce, then.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:54.070
And a funnel and a pot at the 100-yen shop.

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:09.460
We made it!

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:11.630
<i>Lake Yamanaka.</i>

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:14.490
<i>The southeasternmost of the Fuji Five Lakes.</i>

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:19.470
<i>At 980 meters above sea level, 
it's also the highest.</i>

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:26.810
<b>Welcome to Lake Yamanaka</b>

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:26.810
<i>It's a popular tourist area, and is shaped 
like a whale when north is at the top.</i>

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:29.760
It looks more like roast 
chicken than a whale to me.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.350
<i>I see it.</i>

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:36.950
Looks like there's a place called 
Hammocker's Café by the lakeside.

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:39.520
Want to go check it out tomorrow or so?

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:45.430
"Come sway in our hammocks 
as you drift off into a nap."

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:47.460
Wow, that sounds nice.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:50.210
Closed during the winter.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:50.210
Lodging\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hDining\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hEvents

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:49.520
Oh...

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:57.970
H-Hey, there's still the tour boat, 
the art gallery, and the shops.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:02.090
There's a lot to see within walking 
distance of the campsite.

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:03.220
Yeah.

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:06.740
Sorry! The place I booked is 
on the other side of the lake.

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:08.980
There's nothing in the area.

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:17.510
S-Still, it's a pretty nice place.

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:18.640
You sure?

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:19.610
You sure?

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.370
Pardon me...

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:27.370
Do you know how to get to Hiranu Hut Springs?

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:30.060
Hiranu Hut Springs?

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:33.000
Oh, Hirano Hot Springs!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:36.510
Hiranu Hut Springs is two stops uhead.

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:39.260
Why'd you have to do the accent?

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:40.960
Thank you.

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:42.810
You're wulcome.

00:18:46.380 --> 00:18:49.690
Lots of people from abroad 
at the tourist traps, huh?

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:52.440
That's the puwer of Mt. Fuji.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:53.400
Stop.

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:56.460
Hang on, what were we talking about again?

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:59.280
We were saying that 
Nadeshiko-chan is wife to us all.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:00.910
You went too far back.

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:03.410
There it is. Over there.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:07.660
Most of the campsites around here 
are in the woods or by the lakeside.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:13.230
We're going to Cape Ohmama Campsite,
the only place you can stay on the cape.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.180
<b>Bus Waiting Area</b>

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:31.140
<b>Cape Ohmama Campsite
 Fishing Spot Entrance
 Rental Boats, Bicycles, Fishing Tickets
 Tennis Court Rentals  
Eatery, Shops, Parking</b>

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:35.820
<b>No Parking</b>

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:43.950
<b>Cape
Ohmama
Campsite</b>

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:45.410
<b>Paid Parking</b>

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:52.400
This is such a nice spot!

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.370
It is! This is awesome!

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:55.590
Isn't it?

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:14.600
Finally, huh?

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:15.770
Yeah.

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:18.220
Time to start camping.

00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:19.110
Yeah.

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:24.230
Don't get too excited just yet.

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:27.990
I bet if we set up over there 
at the end of the cape,

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:34.280
it'll feel like we're camping 
in the middle of the lake.

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:38.280
Camping in the middle of the lake...

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:46.260
Let's go get registration over with and try 
out our new camping chairs on the cape.

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:48.980
Yeah, totally!

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:55.640
You can't pitch your tents
 at the end of the cape!

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:57.520
That's dangerous!

00:22:33.060 --> 00:22:35.540
<b>Shima Shima Shima Rin</b>

00:22:33.480 --> 00:22:35.540
<i>Shima Shima Shima Rin.</i>

00:22:36.650 --> 00:22:39.960
<i>One day, while I was camping...</i>

00:22:42.230 --> 00:22:43.720
That's some good acorn.

00:22:44.180 --> 00:22:45.550
<i>I realized that I could hear...</i>

00:22:45.860 --> 00:22:47.520
It's chilly today, huh?

00:22:47.520 --> 00:22:49.220
It's going to rain soon.

00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:52.050
<i>...what the animals and trees were saying.</i>

00:22:52.290 --> 00:22:53.370
Hello.

00:22:53.370 --> 00:22:54.270
Hiya.

00:22:54.270 --> 00:22:55.080
'Sup!

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:56.250
Hello.

00:22:56.250 --> 00:22:57.060
Yo!

00:22:57.250 --> 00:22:59.080
Hello...

00:22:59.560 --> 00:23:00.310
Ah!

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:01.470
Help!

00:23:01.470 --> 00:23:02.430
Kyah!

00:23:02.430 --> 00:23:03.540
Ah!

00:23:03.540 --> 00:23:04.320
No!

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:14.330
Kyah!

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:14.330
Aiee!

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:14.330
Eek!

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:14.330
Stop!

00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:14.330
Urgh!

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:14.330
It burns!

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:14.330
Nooo!

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:14.330
Help!

00:23:12.410 --> 00:23:14.330
Hidebu!

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:16.330
Why?!

00:23:19.570 --> 00:23:20.330
Save me!

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:23.750
<i>Just a dream...</i>

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:35.140
<b>Cape Ohmama in Winter</b>

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:35.140
